      <header class="article-header">
        <span class="article-header__tag">Tools</span>
        <h1>10 Best AI Tools for LinkedIn Personal Branding in 2026</h1>
        <p class="article-header__meta">September 2026 · 10 min read · By <a href="https://perchd.space" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px;">Perchd</a></p>
        <p class="article-header__deck">Nearly every "best LinkedIn tools" roundup is published by one of the tools on it. We checked a dozen of them while researching this piece, and the pattern held almost every time. This list includes Perchd — since we built it — but we're not ranking it first by default, and we're naming where competitors are genuinely stronger.</p>
      </header>

      <div class="article-cover">
        <img src="/blog-cover-ai-tools-linkedin.jpg" alt="A laptop showing a LinkedIn profile dashboard with AI content assistant, headline ideas, and content inspiration panels — illustrating AI tools for LinkedIn personal branding" width="1200" height="675">
      </div>

      <div class="article-body">
        <p>The market for LinkedIn content tools has expanded fast. In 2026, there are at least a dozen tools with genuine traction, and their marketing claims are almost uniformly superlative. Sorting them requires being specific about what you're actually trying to solve — and honest about where each tool falls short. That's what this list is trying to do.</p>

        <p>If you want the broader context on <em>why</em> LinkedIn personal branding has become worth taking seriously as a channel, we covered the data behind that in <a href="/blog/2026-state-of-founder-personal-branding">The 2026 State of Founder Personal Branding</a>. This piece is specifically about the tools.</p>

        <div class="callout">A note on placement: Perchd is #10 on this list, not because it's the weakest option, but because it's a different category of tool — one that only makes sense once you've understood what the others do and don't solve. Read the full entry before drawing conclusions from the number.</div>

        <!-- Tool 1 -->
        <div class="tool-card">
          <p class="tool-card__number">No. 1</p>
          <p class="tool-card__name">Taplio</p>
          <div class="tool-card__body">
            <p>The most established name in this space, and the closest thing to an all-in-one suite: AI post generation, a large library of high-performing posts to draw inspiration from, a scheduler, analytics, and a lightweight CRM for tracking who's engaging with you.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-card__screenshot">
            <img src="/tool-taplio.webp" alt="Taplio platform showing 'Grow your personal brand on LinkedIn in 10 minutes a day' with user avatars from 2500+ LinkedIn creators, consultants, and CEOs using the tool" width="800" height="534" loading="lazy">
          </div>
          <div class="tool-card__meta">
            <div class="tool-card__meta-row">
              <span class="tool-card__meta-label">Pricing</span>
              <span>Advertised from $39/month, but the AI writing features that make it worth using sit behind a roughly $65–$69/month tier.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tool-card__meta-row">
              <span class="tool-card__meta-label">Best for</span>
              <span>Founders who want content, scheduling, analytics, and light outreach CRM all in one dashboard, and don't mind paying suite pricing for that breadth.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-card__caveat"><strong>Honest caveat:</strong> It's built more as a growth and lead-gen suite than a pure content-quality tool, so if voice authenticity is your main concern, it's not the strongest option on this list for that specifically.</div>
        </div>

        <!-- Tool 2 -->
        <div class="tool-card">
          <p class="tool-card__number">No. 2</p>
          <p class="tool-card__name">Bloomberry</p>
          <div class="tool-card__body">
            <p>Built around the deepest voice-modeling approach we found. Instead of learning from a handful of recent posts, it analyzes your full existing body of work to capture sentence patterns, vocabulary, and structural habits — then turns one idea into LinkedIn posts, X threads, and blog articles in that voice.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-card__screenshot">
            <img src="/tool-bloomberry.webp" alt="Bloomberry platform showing employee-led growth dashboard with campaign voices, CEO and writer roles, posts ready for approval, and performance metrics including 4.2x engagement and 1k+ reach" width="1400" height="768" loading="lazy">
          </div>
          <div class="tool-card__meta">
            <div class="tool-card__meta-row">
              <span class="tool-card__meta-label">Pricing</span>
              <span>Mid-range subscription; check current tiers directly, as they've shifted more than once this year.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tool-card__meta-row">
              <span class="tool-card__meta-label">Best for</span>
              <span>Founders who already have a lot of existing writing — old posts, blog content, transcripts — and want a tool that actually learns from all of it rather than a thin sample.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-card__caveat"><strong>Honest caveat:</strong> The depth of the voice model is the whole value proposition here, so it's less useful if you're starting from a blank slate with little existing content to train on.</div>
        </div>

        <!-- Tool 3 -->
        <div class="tool-card">
          <p class="tool-card__number">No. 3</p>
          <p class="tool-card__name">ViralBrain</p>
          <div class="tool-card__body">
            <p>Combines voice-matched writing with what it calls "hero analysis" — studying top creators in your specific niche — plus a pre-publish score estimating how likely a given post is to perform well.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-card__screenshot">
            <img src="/tool-viralbrain.webp" alt="ViralBrain homepage showing LinkedIn profile URL analysis input, hero post learning from viral patterns, and 4,915 creators analyzed — demonstrating its niche creator intelligence approach" width="1400" height="860" loading="lazy">
          </div>
          <div class="tool-card__meta">
            <div class="tool-card__meta-row">
              <span class="tool-card__meta-label">Pricing</span>
              <span>Comparable to Taplio's mid-tier.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tool-card__meta-row">
              <span class="tool-card__meta-label">Best for</span>
              <span>Founders who want data-driven feedback on a draft before publishing, not just a tool that generates one.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-card__caveat"><strong>Honest caveat:</strong> Like most tools on this list, ViralBrain's own marketing ranks it the best overall option. Judge that claim against your own use case rather than taking it at face value — same as we're asking you to do with Perchd's placement here.</div>
        </div>

        <!-- Tool 4 -->
        <div class="tool-card">
          <p class="tool-card__number">No. 4</p>
          <p class="tool-card__name">Supergrow</p>
          <div class="tool-card__body">
            <p>The clearest budget option that still focuses specifically on writing quality rather than a full suite. Give it a topic and it drafts posts, carousels, and comments from templates.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-card__screenshot">
            <img src="/tool-supergrow.png" alt="Supergrow dashboard showing post generator, idea generator, carousel maker, voice notes, and scheduling tools — used by 8000+ professionals to build a standout LinkedIn personal brand" width="1512" height="792" loading="lazy">
          </div>
          <div class="tool-card__meta">
            <div class="tool-card__meta-row">
              <span class="tool-card__meta-label">Pricing</span>
              <span>Roughly $19–$39/month, among the cheapest tools with real AI drafting features.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tool-card__meta-row">
              <span class="tool-card__meta-label">Best for</span>
              <span>Solo creators and early-stage founders who want AI help with the blank page without paying for scheduling and analytics they won't use.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-card__caveat"><strong>Honest caveat:</strong> Thinner voice-modeling than Bloomberry or ViralBrain, since the focus is speed and price rather than depth.</div>
        </div>

        <!-- Tool 5 -->
        <div class="tool-card">
          <p class="tool-card__number">No. 5</p>
          <p class="tool-card__name">Kleo</p>
          <div class="tool-card__body">
            <p>Worth knowing the backstory: the original Kleo was a Chrome extension that analyzed other people's posts, until LinkedIn issued a cease-and-desist over data scraping and shut it down. Kleo 2.0 is a different product built around AI post generation, voice training, a knowledge base, and scheduling.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-card__screenshot">
            <img src="/tool-kleo.jpeg" alt="Kleo logo — AI-powered LinkedIn content tool rebuilt after the original Chrome extension was shut down by LinkedIn" width="1200" height="630" loading="lazy">
          </div>
          <div class="tool-card__meta">
            <div class="tool-card__meta-row">
              <span class="tool-card__meta-label">Pricing</span>
              <span>Around $99/month with no free trial — currently the steepest entry cost of the tools on this list.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tool-card__meta-row">
              <span class="tool-card__meta-label">Best for</span>
              <span>Teams or serious solo creators who want a knowledge-base-driven workflow and can justify the price.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-card__caveat"><strong>Honest caveat:</strong> At $99/month with no free plan, tools like Supergrow or RedactAI offer comparable AI voice training for a fraction of the cost if budget matters to you.</div>
        </div>

        <!-- Tool 6 -->
        <div class="tool-card">
          <p class="tool-card__number">No. 6</p>
          <p class="tool-card__name">AuthoredUp</p>
          <div class="tool-card__body">
            <p>Less a generation engine and more a serious editor and formatting tool: line breaks, emoji placement, hook previews, and post analytics — the details that affect readability more than most people realize.</p>
            <p>If you've read our piece on <a href="/blog/2026-state-of-founder-personal-branding">how LinkedIn's algorithm now weighs dwell time over reaction counts</a>, you'll understand why formatting matters more than it used to. AuthoredUp is the tool most directly built around that.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-card__screenshot">
            <img src="/tool-authoredup.png" alt="AuthoredUp editor showing a LinkedIn post draft with readability score, live mobile preview, hooks and endings tabs, and character count — highlighting its focus on formatting and readability over raw content generation" width="1456" height="816" loading="lazy">
          </div>
          <div class="tool-card__meta">
            <div class="tool-card__meta-row">
              <span class="tool-card__meta-label">Pricing</span>
              <span>Modest — positioned as a companion tool rather than a full suite.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tool-card__meta-row">
              <span class="tool-card__meta-label">Best for</span>
              <span>Founders who already know what they want to say and want to make sure it's formatted for maximum readability before it goes out.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-card__caveat"><strong>Honest caveat:</strong> It won't help you figure out what to write. It's specifically for polishing something you've already drafted.</div>
        </div>

        <!-- Tool 7 -->
        <div class="tool-card">
          <p class="tool-card__number">No. 7</p>
          <p class="tool-card__name">Shield</p>
          <div class="tool-card__body">
            <p>A dedicated analytics layer, frequently paired with a separate content tool rather than used alone — since it doesn't generate posts itself. Brings a depth of performance data that the built-in LinkedIn analytics don't come close to matching.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-card__screenshot">
            <img src="/tool-shield.webp" alt="Shield analytics dashboard showing LinkedIn performance metrics including 947,443 views (+3,794%), 6,162 likes, 590 comments, 0.72% engagement rate, earned media value of $7,580, and top posts breakdown by views" width="1040" height="700" loading="lazy">
          </div>
          <div class="tool-card__meta">
            <div class="tool-card__meta-row">
              <span class="tool-card__meta-label">Pricing</span>
              <span>Positioned as an add-on in most creator stacks, typically bringing a full stack to around $50/month combined with a content tool and a design tool like Canva.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tool-card__meta-row">
              <span class="tool-card__meta-label">Best for</span>
              <span>Founders who want genuinely deep performance data and are willing to run it alongside a separate writing tool.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-card__caveat"><strong>Honest caveat:</strong> You'll need something else for the actual content creation — this solves one layer only.</div>
        </div>

        <!-- Tool 8 -->
        <div class="tool-card">
          <p class="tool-card__number">No. 8</p>
          <p class="tool-card__name">RedactAI</p>
          <div class="tool-card__body">
            <p>The cheapest dedicated voice-training tool we found in current use, positioned directly as a lower-cost alternative to pricier options like Kleo.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-card__screenshot">
            <img src="/tool-redactai.jpeg" alt="RedactAI homepage showing AI LinkedIn post creation with 100% personalized content tailored to your unique style — used by 10,000+ LinkedIn creators, with a free starter plan requiring no credit card" width="900" height="600" loading="lazy">
          </div>
          <div class="tool-card__meta">
            <div class="tool-card__meta-row">
              <span class="tool-card__meta-label">Pricing</span>
              <span>Around $11.90/month.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tool-card__meta-row">
              <span class="tool-card__meta-label">Best for</span>
              <span>Anyone testing whether AI-assisted writing is worth paying for at all, before committing to a pricier tool.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-card__caveat"><strong>Honest caveat:</strong> You generally get what you pay for in depth of voice modeling — treat this as an entry point rather than a long-term solution once your content strategy matures.</div>
        </div>

        <!-- Tool 9 -->
        <div class="tool-card">
          <p class="tool-card__number">No. 9</p>
          <p class="tool-card__name">Oiti</p>
          <div class="tool-card__body">
            <p>One of the newer entrants, built around a deep persona document — reportedly around 3,000 words — generated from your last 100 posts, your website, and research into your ideal customer profile, then used to ground every draft it produces.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-card__screenshot">
            <img src="/tool-oiti.webp" alt="Oiti homepage — self-learning AI LinkedIn ghostwriter that transforms conversations, voice notes, articles, and meetings into long-form LinkedIn posts in seconds" width="1512" height="820" loading="lazy">
          </div>
          <div class="tool-card__meta">
            <div class="tool-card__meta-row">
              <span class="tool-card__meta-label">Pricing</span>
              <span>$49–$79/month, with early-adopter annual discounts currently available.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tool-card__meta-row">
              <span class="tool-card__meta-label">Best for</span>
              <span>Founders who want the tool to actually understand their business and audience, not just their writing style.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-card__caveat"><strong>Honest caveat:</strong> It's new enough that the long-term track record is thinner than more established names on this list.</div>
        </div>

        <!-- Tool 10 -->
        <div class="tool-card">
          <p class="tool-card__number">No. 10</p>
          <p class="tool-card__name">Perchd <span style="font-size:0.7em;font-weight:500;color:var(--muted);">(disclosure: this is our product)</span></p>
          <div class="tool-card__body">
            <p>A different category of tool — worth being upfront about. Everything above is a content-generation tool: you're still the one deciding what to say and largely still the one finalizing it. Perchd starts a step earlier, with an actual strategy interview that builds your <a href="/#how">positioning and audience</a> before any content gets written.</p>
            <p>From there, it splits the ongoing work into two separate jobs: AI handles the weekly strategy and drafting, and a real person — you, or a writer we pair you with depending on your plan — finishes the actual sentences.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-card__meta">
            <div class="tool-card__meta-row">
              <span class="tool-card__meta-label">Pricing</span>
              <span>$79/month (Starter) up to $199/month (Pro) for AI-plus-self-write and AI-plus-edit tiers, or from $1,800/month (Agency) if you want it fully handled by a human writer. <a href="/#pricing">See full plans →</a></span>
            </div>
            <div class="tool-card__meta-row">
              <span class="tool-card__meta-label">Best for</span>
              <span>Founders who don't just want faster content, but want the underlying strategy done properly first — and who want the option to hand off the actual writing entirely rather than always doing a final edit pass themselves.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="tool-card__caveat"><strong>Honest caveat:</strong> If all you want is a faster way to draft posts and you already know exactly what your positioning and voice should be, several of the tools above are cheaper and more focused on pure content speed. Perchd is built for the strategy gap specifically — not to be the cheapest drafting tool on this list.</div>
        </div>

        <h2>Which one should you actually pick?</h2>
        <p>That depends almost entirely on which specific problem you're trying to solve. Here's the honest version:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>If you want the cheapest way to test AI-assisted writing</strong> — start with <strong>RedactAI</strong> or <strong>Supergrow</strong>. Both give you enough to judge whether the format works for you without a meaningful financial commitment.</li>
          <li><strong>If you already have a large body of existing writing</strong> and want the deepest voice match — <strong>Bloomberry</strong> is the strongest option we found for that specifically.</li>
          <li><strong>If you want an all-in-one suite</strong> with built-in CRM, outreach, and content — <strong>Taplio</strong> remains the most complete single-dashboard option.</li>
          <li><strong>If formatting and readability are your weak spot</strong>, not the ideas themselves — <strong>AuthoredUp</strong> is the most focused tool for that layer.</li>
          <li><strong>If you want serious analytics without switching content tools</strong> — <strong>Shield</strong> pairs cleanly with most of the above.</li>
          <li><strong>If the actual problem is that you don't know what your positioning should be</strong> in the first place — none of the pure content tools above solve that. That's the specific gap <a href="/#how">Perchd</a> is built to close.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="callout">The one thing every tool on this list has in common: they work better when the underlying strategy is clear. If you're posting without a defined point of view and a specific audience in mind, better tooling mostly just helps you produce the wrong content faster. Sort that first.</div>

        <p>For more on what "the right content" actually looks like in 2026 — including how LinkedIn's algorithm has shifted and why topical consistency now matters more than posting volume — see <a href="/blog/2026-state-of-founder-personal-branding">The 2026 State of Founder Personal Branding</a>.</p>

        <div class="sources">
